/datum/faith/old_god
	name = "Psydonism"
	desc = "Omnipotent and omniscient yet speaking only through angels and prophets, Psydon's enigmas confound mortal theologians to this day. Fractured in the current era across several schisms, the ancient scriptures that all agree upon were clear; Psydon created form from nothingness, divided the Firmament from the Heavens, and imbued the Firmament with Lux. The Ten Divines were formed thereafter, created to govern His creation and granted powers over the Lux that remained. Beyond this foundational truth comes questions of false prophets and errant scribes; the search for perfection in faith is a crucible to burn away falsehoods. It has become apparent that false prophets and heretics grow more common by the century, and precisely when Psydon last gave a true message to a mortal mind is wholly unknown. The chaos of recent centuries bring the old faith into question; not only are the Ascendants claiming godhead and mortals believing divine power could be usurped for all, but the Divines themselves, bereft of authoritative messages from Psydon's angels, slowly turn from one another with frighteningly mortal fears. For if Psydon could perish, what hope have they? What is clear is that He has fallen silent, nothing more than a wordless whisper in the dark or a stirring of the heart at a poignant moment. But those who believe, ENDURE. "
	godhead = /datum/patron/old_god
